---
import LegalLayout from "../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy — AzmFit"
  description="How AzmFit collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: [DATE]</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> AzmFit collects only what's
      needed to make the app work — your account, what you log, and
      (with your permission) Apple Health data. We don't sell your data,
      we don't share it with advertisers, and you can delete it any
      time from inside the app.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit is operated by <strong>[COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME]</strong>
    ("AzmFit," "we," "us"). This policy explains what data we collect
    when you use the AzmFit iOS app or visit azmfit.co, how we use it,
    and your rights over it.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have questions, contact us at
    <strong>[CONTACT_EMAIL]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>

  <h3>Account information</h3>
  <p>
    When you create an account, we collect your email address, a
    hashed password, your name (if you provide one), and your
    preferred language.
  </p>

  <h3>Profile information you enter</h3>
  <p>
    Your date of birth, biological sex, height, weight, activity
    level, and fitness goal — used to compute personalized calorie and
    macro targets. You can change or delete any of these from Settings.
  </p>

  <h3>Workout and meal logs</h3>
  <p>
    Every workout you record (exercises, sets, weights, reps, notes)
    and every meal you log (food items, quantities, macros) is stored
    so it can appear in your history, charts, and Fitness Level.
  </p>

  <h3>Apple Health data (with your permission)</h3>
  <p>
    If you grant Apple Health access, we read steps, active energy,
    sleep duration and stages, and resting heart rate. This data
    syncs into your AzmFit account so it can power the Fitness Level
    score and weekly digest. We do not write back to Apple Health
    without your explicit action.
  </p>

  <h3>Subscription information</h3>
  <p>
    If you subscribe to Personal Pro or Coach Pro, we receive a
    transaction identifier from Apple via RevenueCat (our subscription
    management provider). We never see or store your payment card
    details — those are handled entirely by Apple.
  </p>

  <h3>Coaching data (Coach Pro users only)</h3>
  <p>
    If you connect with a coach inside the app, that coach can see
    your workouts, meals, weight, and other logs you choose to share.
    Coaches can leave notes on your sessions. You can end a coaching
    relationship from Settings at any time, which immediately revokes
    the coach's access.
  </p>

  <h3>Device and usage information</h3>
  <p>
    We collect basic device information (OS version, app version,
    language, region) and anonymous usage events (e.g., which screens
    you open) to diagnose crashes and improve the product. We do not
    track you across other apps or websites.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the core features: log workouts and meals, render
      charts, compute your Fitness Level, generate weekly digests.</li>
    <li>To process subscriptions and enforce tier limits (e.g., AI
      quota, custom food count).</li>
    <li>To send AI-generated weekly digests (you can disable this in
      Settings).</li>
    <li>To diagnose bugs and improve app performance.</li>
    <li>To respond to your support requests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. AI-powered features</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit uses OpenAI to power the AI quick-log feature and the
    weekly digest. When you use these features, the relevant text
    (e.g., your meal description, or a summary of your weekly stats)
    is sent to OpenAI's API for processing. OpenAI does not retain
    this data for training, per their API data usage policy. We do
    not send your personal identifiers (name, email) along with these
    requests.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How we share your information</h2>
  <p>We share data only with the following categories of recipients:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> who help us run the app:
      Supabase (backend hosting and database), RevenueCat (subscription
      management), OpenAI (AI features), Apple (App Store delivery and
      payment).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your coach</strong>, if you have an active coaching
      relationship inside the app (and only the data they can see in
      their coach view).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal authorities</strong>, if required by valid legal
      process (we will challenge requests we believe are overly broad).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We never sell your data, share it with advertisers, or
    use it to build targeted-ad profiles.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>6. Where your data is stored</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit data is stored in Supabase's [REGION] region. By using the
    app, you consent to this storage location. We protect data in
    transit with TLS and at rest with industry-standard encryption.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep your data</h2>
  <p>
    We retain your account and logs for as long as your account is
    active. When you delete your account from Settings, we delete
    your personal data within 30 days, except where retention is
    required by law (e.g., financial records for tax purposes).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of your data.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> — fix any inaccurate information
      (most fields are editable directly in the app).</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> — delete your account and all
      associated data from Settings → Account → Delete Account.</li>
    <li><strong>Export</strong> — request a portable copy of your
      data by emailing [CONTACT_EMAIL].</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — revoke Apple Health
      access from iOS Settings → Health → Sharing → AzmFit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly
    collect data from anyone under 13. If you believe a child has
    created an account, contact us at [CONTACT_EMAIL] and we will
    delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes
    will be announced in-app at least 30 days before they take effect.
    The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most
    recent change.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, requests, or concerns? Email us at
    <strong>[CONTACT_EMAIL]</strong>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
